node_modules
dist
.git
.github

# `*.md` is ROOT-LEVEL ONLY — a dockerignore pattern's `*` does not cross a `/`. That matters
# now: `docs/**/*.md` IS part of the build context and must stay that way, because the build
# stage renders it into `dist/knowledge/` via `scripts/knowledge-plugin.mjs`. Excluding
# `docs` and `scripts` (as this file used to) breaks `npm run build` inside the image at the
# point where vite.config.mjs imports the plugin.
#
# Neither directory reaches the runtime image: stage 2 copies dist/, server/, src/core,
# src/data and package.json, and nothing else.
#
# `.git` stays out, so the "last updated" dates fall back to the build stamp in a container
# build. That is why scripts/knowledge.mjs treats a missing git history as normal.
*.md

# Credential-shaped files, mirroring .gitignore.
#
# Nothing here matches anything today and nothing should ever match. The reason to list them
# anyway is that .gitignore does NOT protect a build context: `COPY . .` reads the working
# directory, so a stray local key that git is correctly ignoring would still be baked into an
# image layer and pushed to a registry. Ignoring it in one place and not the other is exactly
# the gap that lets that happen.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*-key.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json
